# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (native from day one — atari800xl wave, 2026-09-08) ----
# MAME 0.289's a800xlp runs ON THE HOST — same engine as apple2e/mpf2,
# drawshm frames, ctlsock keys through the generated keymap, sound -> SDL
# disk -> FIFO with the daemon as clock. Launcher: shared
# stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh; reset = relaunch restoring the golden
# savestate (src/mame/atari/atari400.cpp (MACHINE_IMPERFECT_GRAPHICS; no MACHINE_SUPPORTS_SAVE flag — the golden stream MUST prove SAVEST/LOADST or ship MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=0 with a cold boot to the menu)).
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Atari 800XL, MAME 0.289 a800xlp running HOST-NATIVE (drawshm, no QEMU/QMP). MyPicoDos 4.06N boot menu on the D1: drive (hive.atr, MyDOS SINGLE-density, 92 176 B -- REBUILT from enhanced density 2026-09-08 golden-fix stream: MAME's emulated Atari 1050, src/devices/bus/a800/atari1050.cpp, implements only single/double density, never enhanced, so an ED image drew a correct menu but failed every XEX load) lists BOULDER.XEX, LASTWORD.XEX, LW.CFG, RIVRRAID.XEX, STARRAID.XEX, XBASIC.XEX; DROPZONE.XEX moved to a second single-density drive hive2.atr (D2:, -flop2, 92 176 B, no boot code) because all six D1: entries already fill the 90 K single-density ceiling. Highlight starts on BOULDER.XEX, RETURN loads the highlighted file. Cold boot MEASURED on the golden stream's sandbox rig 2026-09-08: directory fully painted by mtime~19s, first drawn frame at ~6.5s wall; the golden savestate captured at the fully-settled menu restores in 75ms (ctl.sock ready 5ms after relaunch) and is PIXEL-IDENTICAL to the pre-capture frame (PIL bbox None). Navigation MEASURED: the station's PC arrow keys, already mapped by the keymap to :ctrl1:joy:JOY P1 Up/Down/Left/Right (no override needed, no Ctrl chord required despite MyPicoDos's own documented Ctrl+-/=/+/* combo), move the highlight bar one entry per press over ctlsock KEY -- this is the input the on-screen keyboard already offers, so a visitor can move the bar. SOLVED by the golden3 stream (2026-09-08): the long-standing "RETURN does not load a title" wall was NOT the loader, the density or the key transport -- it was ONE BAD TITLE. BOULDER.XEX, the entry the highlight starts on, REBOOTS the machine (its post-RETURN frame hashes are byte-identical to a cold boot: 842 B blue 36c04d58, 402 B boot frame 634e1046 at ~14 s, 2090 B half-painted directory 92f4090b at ~19.8 s, settled 2980 B menu 7ba7f15e at ~21 s), with the Atari BASIC ROM enabled AND with console OPTION held down from power-on. Every earlier stream only ever pressed RETURN on that default entry. Moving the highlight down first PROVES the other titles: 1 down LASTWORD.XEX -> The Last Word 3.2 splash then editor; 3 downs RIVRRAID.XEX -> River Raid attract mode; 4 downs STARRAID.XEX -> the STAR RAIDERS title screen. Boot code is not a variable (MyPicoDos 406/406N/406B/405B/404B/403 all reboot identically on entry 0) and neither is file size (a disk holding only the 18-byte XBASIC.XEX does not reboot). STILL OPEN: BOULDER.XEX must be dropped from or replaced on hive.atr before landing (the broken title is the DEFAULT highlight); XBASIC.XEX does not reach Atari BASIC -- the OS warm start re-enters MyPicoDos through DOSINI and the pixel-identical menu comes back, so DOSINI must be neutralised before JMP $E474; the D2: drive-select key to DROPZONE.XEX is still untested. Media and the staged golden are byte-unchanged from the golden-fix stream.
MAME_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/atari800xl/mame-native/atari800xl
MAME_NATIVE_DRIVER=a800xlp
MAME_NATIVE_ROMS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/atari800xl/mame-native/roms
MAME_NATIVE_GEOM=1024x768
# MEASURED on the native stream's rig (2026-09-08): ui.ini's skip_warnings
# alone does NOTHING upstream (options().skip_warnings() is never
# consulted) — the "known problems: Completely unemulated features: disk /
# Imperfectly emulated features: graphics" panel shows regardless and
# would BE the exhibit. mame-irix-skip-warnings.patch (added to this
# station's NATIVE_EXTRA_PATCHES) makes the option take effect; =1 here is
# required, not optional.
MAME_NATIVE_SKIP_WARNINGS=1
# DECIDED by the golden stream (2026-09-08): =1. SAVEST at the settled menu
# (mtime~19s) and a relaunch with -state golden were proven pixel-identical
# on the sandbox rig (PIL bbox None) and restore in 75 ms vs. a ~19 s cold
# boot -- a real win despite atari400.cpp/a800xlp carrying no
# MACHINE_SUPPORTS_SAVE driver flag. REBAKED by the golden-fix stream
# (2026-09-08) on the new single-density disk pair; golden path staged at
# stations/atari800xl/sta/a800xlp/golden.sta (31 855 B, sha256
# 94eab84d9c91fda52f4c853fec27accddf6f0a550129666399364bcaabe9e64b).
MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=1
# Device set CONFIRMED on the 0.289 build (-listslots a800xlp): the Atari
# 1050 Dual Density Disk Drive is a800xlp's own DEFAULT sio slot, so it is
# left OFF the command line on purpose — MEASURED 2026-09-08: passing
# "-sio a1050" explicitly (even though it names the default) makes THIS
# build silently drop the -flop1..4 media options ("-flop1" then errors as
# an unknown option); omitting -sio keeps the same drive attached AND
# keeps -flop1 working. -ctrl1 joy is the CX40 joystick (arrows + fire via
# the keymap override rows). With hive.atr present (media stream), cold
# boot reaches MyPicoDOS's file menu, proven on the native stream's rig
# (docs/lab/ATARI800XL-WAVE.md); with no disk in -flop1 the XL OS instead
# retries the boot sector forever ("BOOT ERROR" loop) — real Atari
# hardware behaviour for a powered disk drive with no disk, not a bug.
MAME_NATIVE_ARGS=-flop1 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/atari800xl/media/hive.atr -flop2 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/atari800xl/media/hive2.atr -ctrl1 joy
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/atari800xl/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/atari800xl/atari800xl.keymap
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/atari800xl/audio.fifo

SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/atari800xl/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/atari800xl/mame-native
MAME_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# Fleet floor for MAME keyboard stations (playbook §0): measure only if
# characters drop. A CPU-scanned matrix may need MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL=1.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=40
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=40
